  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I experienced a issue. My account was suspended for 7 days, and after returning home from FWA on May 21, 2026, I discovered that both my account and my community group had been penalized for alleged sexual activity violations, despite there being no such activity taking place.\n\nModeration Type: Temporary Suspension\n\nApplied: May 21, 2026, 1:58 PM UTC\n\nExpired: May 28, 2026, 2:58 PM UTC\n\n1 hour after taking my money for vrc+ They banned Account & Group\n\nReason Provided:\n\n\"Your account was found to be in violation of our Adult Sexual Activity and Nudity guidelines. As a result, your account has been suspended for 1 week. Some of your content may have been removed. Please review your account to ensure it is in accordance with our Community Guidelines.\"\n\nOffending Content Listed:\n\nGroup – PrideChaser Crew\n\nCreation Date: July 8, 2023, 10:17 PM UTC\n\nThe issue is that when I requested clarification regarding what specific content violated the guidelines, why the action was taken, and what evidence was used to support the decision, I received nothing more than links to the Community Guidelines. Those links do not explain what content was deemed problematic or what specific action triggered the suspension.\n\nAfter spending a week attempting to obtain answers and receiving little to no meaningful response, I waited for the suspension to expire. Upon returning, I discovered that my group had been removed entirely, again without any specific explanation. I currently have four support tickets that have remained open and unanswered for over a week.\n\nAs a VRChat Plus subscriber, I believe paying customers deserve greater transparency when enforcement actions are taken. If content is removed, a group is deleted, or an account is suspended, users should be provided with a clear explanation identifying the specific content or behavior that violated policy. Simply directing users to broad guideline pages is often too vague to allow someone to understand what happened, correct any issues, or meaningfully appeal a decision.\n\nThe current process leaves users guessing whether the action resulted from a misunderstanding, an inaccurate report, targeted reporting by other users, or an actual policy violation. Transparency and timely communication are essential to maintaining trust between the platform and its community, and I believe improvements are needed in both areas.\n\nAlso remind you the acct was suspended 2 days before FWA for stickers I appealed it and it was released after 12 hours and 3 stickers were removed but as the group has been removed and there not responding to get it back for something I worked hard on for 3 years. Side Note there raked as a F on the Better Business Bureau and filed a complaint with them when your dealing with money transactions you better have staff to help fix issues or your held liable as a business and better have better support",
